ee after 2:00 p.m.  would only keep me awake the entire  night so if you're just like me avoid  drinking coffee in the afternoon and go  for a cup of tea instead I like to  either sip on green tea or chamomile tea  if it has been a long and tiring day one  of my ways to wind down is to soak  myself in a warm bath just about 2 to 3  hours before bedtime I'll soak myself  for 20 to 30 minutes it helps to relax  my muscles and also mine a cozy soak  raises the body temperature slightly and  the immediate cool-down period  afterwards relaxes you this natural drop  in body heat will help you to fall  asleep quicker  you  it's breakfast like a king lunch like a  prince and dinner like a pauper that's a  lot of truth in that saying make dinner  your lightest meal and have an early  dinner as much as I can I try to have my  dinner before 8 p.m. and of course I  just love my soup and noodles having a  big ole spicy meal at night will put  your digestive system hard at work this  may cause heartburn or indigestion  which can keep you awake if at all  you're feeling peckish before bedtime  then just go for a small snack and keep  it below 200 calories center oils and  candles helped me to wind down breathe  better fall asleep faster and wake up  feeling refreshed the easiest way is to  buy fragrant candles you can also mix in  a few drops of essential oil with water  and gently miss your pillow before bed  here's a fun fact smells can also  influence your dreams so try out  different scents then make you happy  relax and give you a sweet dream our  body needs time to shift into sleep mode  so one hour before bedtime  put all your electronic devices away  this includes switching off of a TV  laptop iPad and also mobile phones  I am very easily affected by the noise  vibration or even the slightest glow  from my phone  so when I want to get a quality rest I  like to put my phone on airplane mode  one of the most common reasons a lot of  people can fall asleep is because of  thei